<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Simplify Expressions Using Properties of Exponents: Mini-Lesson Review</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01543</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Simplify Expressions Using Properties of Exponents: Mini-Lesson Review</md:title>
    <md:uuid>14c8faf9-502f-41da-801d-6af160ae90dd</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <note class="mini-lesson-question" id="note-00004">
      <title>Question #1: Simplify Expressions Using Properties of Exponents</title>

      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
        <para id="para-00001"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_OR_U6_Q1"/></para>
        </problem>
        </exercise>    </note>
    </section>

    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Simplify Expressions Using Properties of Exponents</title>
      <para id="para-00002">In this unit, remember to double click on mathematical
        expressions/equations to enlarge, if needed.</para>
      <para id="para-00003">In the expression <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math> :</para>
      <para id="para-00004"><m:math>
          <m:mrow>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00005">The exponent 4 means there are 4 factors of <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00006"><m:math>
          <m:mrow>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00007">The exponent 2 means there are 2 factors of <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00008"><m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00009">There are 6 factors of <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>, which can be written as <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>6</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00010"><m:math>
          <m:mrow>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>6</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00011">Notice the exponent is the sum of the exponents of the factors.</para>
      <para id="para-00012">When you multiply exponential expressions with the same base, you keep
        the base and add the exponents.</para>
      <note id="note-00001">
        <title>Product Property for Exponents</title>
  
  <para id="para-00014">If <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> is a real number and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>n</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> are integers, then</para>
  <para id="para-00015"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para><para id="para-00016">To multiply with like bases, add the exponents.</para>
      </note>

      <para id="para-00017">In the expression <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mfrac>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:mfrac>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>
        :</para>
      <para id="para-00018"><m:math>
          <m:mrow>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>5</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00019">The exponent 5 means there are 5 factors of <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00020"><m:math>
          <m:mrow>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00021">The exponent 3 means there are 3 factors of <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00022"><m:math>
          <m:mfrac>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>5</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
          </m:mfrac>
          <m:mo>=</m:mo>
          <m:mfrac>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mo>·</m:mo>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mo>·</m:mo>
              <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              </m:menclose>
              <m:mo>·</m:mo>
              <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              </m:menclose>
              <m:mo>·</m:mo>
              <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              </m:menclose>
            </m:mrow>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              </m:menclose>
              <m:mo>·</m:mo>
              <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              </m:menclose>
              <m:mo>·</m:mo>
              <m:menclose notation="updiagonalstrike">
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              </m:menclose>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:mfrac>
          <m:mo>=</m:mo>
          <m:mi>y</m:mi>
          <m:mo>·</m:mo>
          <m:mi>y</m:mi>
        </m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00023">There are 2 factors of <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>, which can be written as <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00024"><m:math>
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mfrac>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:mfrac>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00025">Notice the exponent is the difference of the exponents of the factors.</para>
      <para id="para-00026">When you divide exponential expressions with the same base, you keep the
        base and subtract the exponents.</para>

      <note id="note-00002">
        <title>Quotient Property for Exponents</title>
  
  <para id="para-00028">If <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> is a real number, <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mo>≠</m:mo>
              <m:mn>0</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>, and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>n</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> are integers, then</para>
  <para id="para-00029"><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
        , <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              <m:mo>></m:mo>
              <m:mi>n</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                      <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                      <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
        , <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>n</m:mi>
              <m:mo>></m:mo>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
      </note>

      <para id="para-00030">Here’s how to simplify expressions using properties of exponents.</para>
      <para id="para-00067">1. <m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>

      <para id="para-00031">The bases are the same. To multiply, use the Product Property for
        Exponents.</para>
      <para id="para-00032"><m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mn>5</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>. To multiply
        with like bases, add the exponents.</para>
      <para id="para-00068">2. <m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>

      <para id="para-00033">The bases are the same. To multiply, use the Product Property for
        Exponents.</para>
      <para id="para-00034">Remember: A variable with no exponent shown has an exponent of <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mn>1</m:mn>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>, <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>1</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00035"><m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>1</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mn>5</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>. To multiply
        with like bases, add the exponents.</para>
      <para id="para-00069">3. <m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00036">The bases are the same. To divide, use the Quotient Property of
        Exponents.</para>
      <para id="para-00037"><m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mfrac>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:mfrac>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>. To divide
        with like bases, subtract the exponents.</para>
      <para id="para-00070">4. <m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                  <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00038">The expression contains like bases. Use the Quotient Property of
        Exponents.</para>
      <para id="para-00039"><m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mfrac>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mi>z</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mi>z</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:mfrac>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mfrac>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:mfrac>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mfrac>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:mfrac>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mfrac>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>0</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:mfrac>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mfrac>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            </m:mfrac>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>. To divide
        with like bases, subtract the exponents.</para>
      <para id="para-00040">Remember: Any nonzero number to the zero power is 1.</para>

      <note class="try" id="note-00003">
        <title>Try It: Simplify Expressions Using Properties of Exponents</title>
<exercise id="exer-00001">
          <problem id="prob-00001">

            <para id="para-00041">Simplify the expressions.</para>


            <para id="para-00042"><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00043">Write down your answers. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
        button to compare your work.</para>

          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00044">Here is how to simplify expressions using properties of exponents.</para>

            <para id="para-00045"><m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:msup>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>.
        To multiply with like bases, add the exponents.</para>

          </solution>
        </exercise>


<exercise id="exer-00002">
          <problem id="prob-00002">

            <para id="para-00046"><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>9</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00047">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
        button to compare your work.</para>

          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00048">Compare your answer: </para>

            <para id="para-00049"><m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>9</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>9</m:mn>
                      <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:msup>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>.
        To divide with like bases, subtract the exponents.</para>


          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <!--Q#2-->
        <!--Interaction
        End -->
<exercise id="exer-00003">
          <problem id="prob-00003">

            <para id="para-00050"><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00051">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
        button to compare your work.</para>

          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00052">Compare your answer: </para>

            <para id="para-00053"><m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                          <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                          <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:msup>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                          <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                          <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                          <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                          <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>.
        To divide with like bases, subtract the exponents.</para>

          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <!--Q#3-->
        <!--Interaction
        End -->

      </note>
    </section>
      <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00003">
        <title>Check Your Understanding</title>
        <exercise id="d195dacc-9ba7-4549-9592-a1cf623a1447" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00054">Which expression is equivalent to <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>
              ?</para>
            <para id="para-00055">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <list list-type="enumerated" number-style="lower-alpha" id="list-00001">
            <item><para id="para-00056"><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></para></item>
            <item><para id="para-00057"><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                    <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></para></item>
           <item> <para id="para-00058"><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></para></item>
            <item><para id="para-00059"><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mfrac>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup>
                        <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                        <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                      </m:msup>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:mfrac>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></para></item>
            </list>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00060">Try again. Take a moment to think about what you learned in the
              mini-lesson review.</para>
              <para id="para-00066">Correct!</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
